    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ba461a7_0cc4284b",
        "filename": "src/base/SkVx.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 215,
      "author": {
        "id": 3375938
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-04T19:59:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is not strictly necessary. I could just fix the one violation I know of in SkMatrix.cpp by initializing the hi float: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/core/SkMatrix.cpp;l\u003d1002;drc\u003d331c38bbbbba75976d99afaa5b456cdbd44939a5\n\nNote that per the C++ standard, passing uninitialized data as parameters (or as a return value) *is* undefined behaviour, so I think the MSan violation is correct.\n\nAs for why fixing it here rather than just one specific instance:\n- There have been very few times when people have been pleasantly surprised by the result of not initializing trivial variables.\n- Projects are increasingly using `-ftrivial-auto-var-init\u003dpattern` or `-ftrivial-auto-var-init\u003dzero`, so they already pay the cost. Chrome uses this flag, for instance.\n- There is some work to continue improving dead store elimination, which will help (but probably not eliminate all cases).\n\nPlaying whack-a-mole isn\u0027t the overall strategy we\u0027ve adopted; we have decided that the very low cost of initializing memory is better than accidentally operating on garbage.\n\nNote that there are ways to opt out of this (i.e. by using https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:base/compiler_specific.h;l\u003d303;drc\u003dc077a30ed629e1389043c1688eea88b9b38a8cf6 when) when there is a demonstrated regression.",
      "parentUuid": "c242125f_9424cabf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 215,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 215,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "7f190dd04a7ad98850854fdc0209640ffe411942",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "24163447_7e2be99d",
        "filename": "src/base/SkVx.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 215,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-04T20:08:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the abstract, I hear you, but in this particular case, this is the base class of SkVx and underpins most of our vectorization code. By definition it is very performance sensitive because we only use SkVx when it matters. \n\nThe case MSAN caught is totally valid and we can fix it there; I trust it to find future cases just as well.",
      "parentUuid": "1ba461a7_0cc4284b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 215,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 215,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "7f190dd04a7ad98850854fdc0209640ffe411942",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f7eb6aba_bb090ff9",
        "filename": "src/base/SkVx.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
